%% DM26-0670

%% How a signed policy reaches every agent and how it is enforced, as built (2026-11-04, authority-distribution.md, policy-enforcement.md, stage 5b). Catching up is
%% general/authority_snapshot_catchup. Designed, not built, and shaded (policy-enforcement.md, stage 6): aging, the bounded degraded window, the restart into init.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant Sign as polar-sign
    participant GS as polar-git-server<br/>(polar-schedules)
    participant Sch as scheduler<br/>observer and processor
    participant CA as credentials agent<br/>consumer
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Ag as every builder agent<br/>(AuthorityActor, PolicyActor)

    Admin->>Sign: polar-sign runtime --agent credentials-agent --section policy --version N
    Note over Sign: the Cedar text is validated against Polar's schema before signing (polar-sign)
    Sign-->>Admin: the signed document (c:update-policy)
    Admin->>GS: push permanent/... over mTLS
    GS->>Sch: RepoChanged
    Sch->>CA: agent.credentials-agent.configuration (forwarded unverified, the receiver verifies)
    CA->>CA: verify chain, signer's c:update-policy (capability only, Cedar never governs its own authorship),<br/>revocation, version higher, then the schema
    CA->>CA: re-sign as an authority Update with the escrow key, numbered through the ledger, apply locally
    CA->>Bk: publish polar-authority-updates
    Bk->>Bk: its Listener hears it on the way through, only from the identity that may publish it:<br/>the same AuthorityCore, for its own subscribe and publish decisions
    Bk->>Bk: JudgeSubscriptions: each Listener judges its connections' subscriptions again,<br/>and one now refused is dropped
    Bk->>Ag: deliver
    Ag->>Ag: AuthorityCore: published_by is the credentials agent,<br/>key pinned from a certified snapshot, signature, sequence:<br/>SetPolicy to the PolicyActor<br/>(a set that does not validate leaves the old one)
    Note over Ag: a jump in the sequence asks for a<br/>snapshot (authority_snapshot_catchup)

    Note over Bk,Ag: a decision, in the agent and in the broker alike: Cedar first,<br/>the certificate where no policy speaks (both directions)

    loop half an hour with no update
        CA->>Bk: the snapshot republished (REPUBLISH_AFTER), for one that missed an update
        Bk->>Ag: deliver
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over CA,Ag: DESIGNED (policy-enforcement.md, stage 6): the credentials agent is unreachable
    Ag->>Ag: 45 minutes without hearing: ask for a snapshot
    Ag->>Ag: degraded: keep deciding with the cached policy,<br/>the certificate where it is silent
    Ag->>Ag: 90 minutes (POLAR_AUTHORITY_MAX_AGE_SECS):<br/>fail the health check
    Note over Ag: the shutdown pipeline, exit 1, and the pod restarts in place,<br/>polar-init waiting for the credentials<br/>agent (health_rejuvenation)
    end
